KNOWNBUG
word_constant_out_of_range2.smv

outside of its width
^EXIT=2$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Same bug as word_constant_out_of_range1.smv, for a signed word constant:
0sd4_10 does not fit in 4 bits and should be rejected, but
convert_word_constant (smv_typecheck.cpp) silently wraps it (two's
complement) to -6 instead, so init(a) is built from a value the user
never wrote.
